---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ShareRow from '../../components/ShareRow.astro';
import ArticleEndCTA from '../../components/ArticleEndCTA.astro';
import { SITE_URL, ORG_ID, PERSON_ID, SLUGS } from '../../lib/site';

const path = SLUGS.successfulButUnfulfilled;
const title = 'Successful But Unfulfilled: Why Achievement Isn’t Enough';
const description =
  'Successful but unfulfilled is more common at the top than most admit. Why achievement stops satisfying, what the emptiness signals, and the first step out.';

const canonical = new URL(path, SITE_URL).href;

// Article + FAQPage — schema types preserved from the design, enriched with
// entity @ids so the founder/org graph resolves.
const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${canonical}#article`,
    headline: 'Successful But Not Happy? Why Achievement Stopped Being Enough',
    author: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
    publisher: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    about: ['successful but unfulfilled', 'successful but not happy', 'meaning after success'],
    description:
      'Why high achievers feel empty despite success, what the feeling signals, and the first step toward becoming again.',
    mainEntityOfPage: `${canonical}#webpage`,
  },
  {
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Why am I successful but not happy?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Often because you achieved a definition of success you never consciously chose — one inherited from a parent, a culture, or an earlier version of yourself. Hitting someone else's target doesn't satisfy you, and the gap shows up as emptiness. It isn't ingratitude or depression by default; it's a signal that the goal that drove you has run out of meaning and it's time to choose a truer one." } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is it normal to feel empty after achieving success?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Very. It's common enough to have a name — the arrival fallacy — the discovery that reaching the goal doesn't deliver the lasting fulfillment you expected. Among high achievers it's the rule more than the exception. The emptiness is information, not a defect: it points to where your growth has stalled and what needs to change." } },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle="Successful But Not Happy? Why Achievement Stopped Being Enough"
  ogDescription="The emptiness after success isn't ingratitude. It's a signal. Here's what it means."
  bodyBg="#EFE8DA"
  schema={schema}
>
  <SiteHeader
    audience="leaders"
    variant="slim"
    logoHref={SLUGS.leaders}
    contextLink={{ label: 'The Legendary Leader →', href: SLUGS.legendaryLeader }}
  />

  <div style="background:#EFE8DA;color:#1B1810;">
    <article>
      <header style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:52px 32px 0;">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:13px;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:22px;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href={SLUGS.leaders} style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">For Leaders</a><span>/</span><span style="color:#C04A26;">Successful but Unfulfilled</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,54px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:#1B1810;max-width:20ch;">Successful, and quietly not happy. You're not ungrateful — you're getting a signal.</h1>
        <div style="margin-top:28px;background:#F4F0E7;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;border-radius:0 12px 12px 0;padding:24px 26px;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:10px;">The short answer</p>
          <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#2E2A22;">Feeling successful but not fulfilled usually means you reached a definition of success you never actually <em style="font-style:italic;">chose</em> — one handed to you by a parent, a culture, or an earlier you. Hitting someone else's target doesn't satisfy. The emptiness isn't a defect; it's information about what needs to change.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:44px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.72;color:#2E2A22;">
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px;">You're not supposed to feel this way. That's the first thing that makes it hard to talk about. By every external measure you won — the title, the exit, the house, the respect. And in the quiet moments there's a flatness you can't explain and feel guilty for even noticing.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px;">Here's the honest read: you probably climbed a mountain someone else pointed you at. The drive was real, but the <em style="font-style:italic;">summit</em> wasn't yours — so standing on it feels strangely empty. Psychologists call the surprise at the top the arrival fallacy. It's not depression by default and it's not ingratitude. It's the moment an old definition of winning runs out of meaning.</p>
          <p style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:24px;line-height:1.4;color:#1B1810;margin:34px 0;padding-left:22px;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;">The emptiness isn't the problem. It's the invitation. It's asking you to choose a truer next thing — one that's actually yours.</p>
          <p>And that's good news, because it means nothing's broken. You don't need to be fixed; you need to become again. That starts with seeing the beliefs and definitions running you — and deciding which ones you'll keep.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:52px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="background:#15130E;color:#F4F0E7;border-radius:18px;padding:40px 42px;text-align:center;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#E0744A;margin-bottom:14px;">The first step is free</p>
          <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,36px);line-height:1.1;color:#FBF8F1;max-width:24ch;margin:0 auto 16px;">Start by seeing what's actually running you.</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:rgba(244,240,231,0.78);max-width:48ch;margin:0 auto 28px;">A free Mindset Workout — about ten minutes — helps you catch the inherited definitions underneath the flatness. Not sure where you are? The two-minute Legend's Journey shows you.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href={SLUGS.workouts} style="background:#C04A26;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 28px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;">Try a Mindset Workout — free <span>&rarr;</span></a>
            <a href={SLUGS.legendsJourney} style="border:1px solid rgba(244,240,231,0.3);color:#F4F0E7;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 26px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:600;font-size:15.5px;">Find where you are</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0 32px 90px;">
        <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);line-height:1.1;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:28px;">Straight answers</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px;">
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">Is it normal to feel empty after success?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">Very — common enough to have a name, the arrival fallacy: reaching the goal doesn't deliver the fulfillment you expected. Among high achievers it's the rule, not the exception. The feeling is information about where your growth has stalled.</p></div>
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">Is this depression?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">Not necessarily — but it can overlap. Restlessness and a search for meaning are different from clinical depression. If the heaviness is persistent, affects sleep or function, or brings hopelessness, talk to a licensed professional. This work complements care; it doesn't replace it.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!-- internal-linking: keep-reading rail -->
      <section style="max-width:860px;margin:8px auto 0;padding:0 32px 76px;">
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C04A26;margin-bottom:16px;">Keep reading</p>
        <div style="display:grid;gap:12px;">
          <a href="/leaders/leadership-plateau/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Why growth stalls: the leadership plateau</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/whats-next-after-success/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">What's next after you've already made it</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/who-am-i-without-my-title/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Who am I without my title?</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <ArticleEndCTA maxWidth={820} />
      <ShareRow title={title} maxWidth={820} />
</article>
  </div>

  <SiteFooter audience="leaders" variant="slim" />
</BaseLayout>
